From 79cfb5aebbf0417418c2ac25669fade7f3e58ef2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Srinivas Kandagatla <srinivas.kandagatla@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 08:38:51 +0100
Subject: ASoC: SDCA: propagate sdw_slave_read_prop() failure in class_read_prop
Git-commit: 79cfb5aebbf0417418c2ac25669fade7f3e58ef2
Patch-mainline: v7.4-rc1
References: git-fixes

sdw_slave_read_prop() can fail with -ENOMEM; propagate the return
instead of leaving slave->prop partially initialised.

Fixes: 2d877d0659cb ("ASoC: SDCA: Add basic SDCA class driver")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Reviewed-by: Charles Keepax <ckeepax@opensource.cirrus.com>
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Srinivas Kandagatla <srinivas.kandagatla@oss.qualcomm.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20261020073856.1177749-2-srinivas.kandagatla@oss.qualcomm.com
Signed-off-by: Mark Brown <broonie@kernel.org>
Acked-by: Takashi Iwai <tiwai@suse.de>

---
 sound/soc/sdca/sdca_class.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/sdca/sdca_class.c b/sound/soc/sdca/sdca_class.c
index 79fdb672be1d..bcc660aeb739 100644
--- a/sound/soc/sdca/sdca_class.c
+++ b/sound/soc/sdca/sdca_class.c
@@ -27,8 +27,11 @@
 static int class_read_prop(struct sdw_slave *sdw)
 {
 	struct sdw_slave_prop *prop = &sdw->prop;
+	int ret;
 
-	sdw_slave_read_prop(sdw);
+	ret = sdw_slave_read_prop(sdw);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
 
 	prop->use_domain_irq = true;
 	prop->scp_int1_mask = SDW_SCP_INT1_BUS_CLASH | SDW_SCP_INT1_PARITY |
-- 
2.55.0

